### Topic 60 - Service discovery with Eureka
### Start: eureka-server (8761) -> product-service (8081, optional 2nd on 8091) -> order-service (8082)

### 1. Eureka registry as JSON (the dashboard is http://localhost:8761 in a browser)
GET http://localhost:8761/eureka/apps
Accept: application/json

### 2. What does order-service see in the registry for product-service?
GET http://localhost:8082/api/orders/discovery

### 3. Load-balancing demo: 6 calls, see which instance answered each one
GET http://localhost:8082/api/orders/lb-demo

### 4. Place an order (product-service is found BY NAME through Eureka)
POST http://localhost:8082/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": 1,
  "quantity": 2
}

### 5. List orders - look at "productServedBy"
GET http://localhost:8082/api/orders

### 6. product-service instances directly
GET http://localhost:8081/api/products/1

###
GET http://localhost:8091/api/products/1

### 7. EXPERIMENT: stop ALL product-service instances, wait ~15 s, send request 4 again
###    -> 503 "No instances available for product-service"
